# C053 — THE OPEN SERVICE INTERFACE (design-only, 2026-07-01). Operator drove the requirement across four turns:
# "platform.config.ts should carry more info so its author can one-shot a toolfactory-complexity base ... create a COMMON
# INTERFACE that defines what each core service is, so others extend it with custom opts and still give control to the
# platform.config.ts author" -> "brandOpts vs serviceOpts" (per-service axis) -> "globalBrandOpts + globalServiceOpts"
# (global axis) -> "opts should also configure how the services work WITH EACH OTHER, not just within itself" (composition).
# Settled via a 13-agent judge-panel workflow (4 stances -> parallel judge + adversarial-break each -> synthesis, ~969k tok).
# Recorded as ADR C053-open-service-interface-and-composition.md. THE DESIGN (NOT built):
#  (1) COMMON INTERFACE: defineService<SO,BO>({ id, registry?, mount(UNCHANGED union), provision?, deps?, env?, serviceOpts,
#      brandOpts, reads:{globalService,globalBrand}, compose:{exposes:ports, offers:capabilities} }); SO/BO are zod v4
#      schemas via the Standard-Schema interface (zod a peerDependency). The 19 core CATALOG entries become defineService
#      values (dogfood); old CATALOG kept as a DERIVED view + a keys-equality drift assertion (collectEnv/orderServices/
#      buildPackageJson/buildProvisionConfig unchanged).
#  (2) MANIFEST factors into defineSystem (services + serviceOpts + globalServiceOpts + wire = the REUSABLE/PUBLISHABLE
#      template) + defineBrand (brandOpts + globalBrandOpts = thin/SWAPPABLE) + definePlatform({system,brand}); defineSystem
#      is generic over the services TUPLE so serviceOpts + wire endpoints autocomplete off the imported Service objects
#      (variadic-tuple inference, ZERO codegen). Legacy single-object PlatformManifest + definePlatform(manifest) kept forever.
#  (3) NODE opts = a 2x2 matrix: service-axis (serviceOpts/globalServiceOpts -> ENTRY, global entry-inert unless a mount opts
#      in via `reads`) x brand-axis (brandOpts/globalBrandOpts -> wrangler [vars]/env). Precedence: schema-default -> read
#      global -> per-service -> legacy opts[id] LAST/lowest (lint on double-set). Origin fields (auth.mcp.loginPage/…,
#      trustedOrigins) TEMPLATED from globalBrandOpts.baseUrl so a rebrand of the SAME system leaks no prior-brand domain.
#  (4) EDGE opts = COMPOSITION via port/capability DI (operator-CONFIRMED). WireDecl{from:"svc.port",to:"svc.cap",with?,id?}
#      typed against BOTH endpoints (variadic-tuple PortRefs/CapRefs); fan-out = flat array in execution order; resolveWiring
#      validates presence + compatibility + ordering + acyclicity (Kahn topo). THE DECISIVE MECHANISM: a bound edge renders
#      INTO the producer port's EXISTING mount-opt field (e.g. auth.onUserCreated), NEVER a separate post-route wire()
#      statement -> reuses a seam that ALREADY EXISTS in registry/services/auth/auth.ts, no invented singletons, the hook closure gets
#      a real env binding. Zero wires on a port -> no hook field -> byte-identical. Edge params SYSTEM by default; a
#      .meta({brand:true,env:"KEY"}) param is brand-tunable via [vars] with an assertNumber startup guard (no silent NaN).
#  (5) SAFE RENDER = two rails: values only via lit(v)=JSON.stringify(parse(schema,v)) (+ assertJsonSafe); identifiers/code
#      only from the TRUSTED Service def (+ validateIdentifier, fail-closed). Residual trust == what shadcn add already grants.
#  (6) EXTENSION = hybrid: npm companion (type-bearing defineService) load-bearing + a registry `suluk` discovery block
#      EMITTED from the companion (no drift); multi-registry alias map + a duplicate-id guard (community ids dotted).
# BYTE-IDENTITY: the legacy path is a STRICT SUBSET through the SAME renderers; the auth->credits grant is currently a
# hand-edit seam NOT in the generated entry, so no wire -> byte-identical. Gated by a Phase-0 golden snapshot (incl. from the
# INSTALLED published generator = the C051 one-shot). PLAN: Phase 0 golden lock -> 1 dogfood byte-identical -> 2 typed 2x2 +
# system/brand -> 3 composition engine (PIN the env-threading seam here before freezing Port) -> 4 multi-registry + community
# edge rebrand proof -> 5 migrate codemod + publish. OPEN (honest): (a) env threading — auth.ts passes only userId today, the
# seam may need widening; (b) cross-cutting/aspect edges (erasure cascade, contract scope gate) don't fit the pairwise shape
# (left module-internal, not in the entry today); (c) registry-fallback typing degrades to unknown; (d) Mount union ceiling
# (queue/DO/cron); (e) GSO-into-mount codegen. Extends C051; governed by C052 ("own the wiring, npm the logic"). The design
# is operator-RATIFIED on the composition crux but ZERO code is written -> byte-identity + env-threading are asserted-by-
# design, provable only by Phase 0 / Phase 3. Modest ceiling.
# NOW BUILT (2026-07-01, operator "go"): Phases 0-5 shipped in @suluk/platform. Phase 0 GOLDEN LOCK pins the real 18-service
# autotoolfactory output byte-for-byte; 1 dogfooded the 19 core services to defineService (CATALOG a derived view); 2 typed
# 2x2 + defineSystem/defineBrand (a system/brand split of autotoolfactory regenerates BYTE-IDENTICAL; wrong opt = compile
# error); 3 the port/capability composition engine (edge renders INTO auth.onUserCreated mount-opt; env seam PINNED by
# widening registry/auth onUserCreated to (userId, env)); 4 community composition + multi-registry + the env seam EMPIRICALLY
# typecheck-verified (generated wired entry over autotoolfactory's real modules -> tsc clean bar the pre-existing
# openapi-compat nit); 5 liftLegacy migrate (round-trips byte-identical) + README + published @suluk/platform 0.2.0. An
# 11-agent ADVERSARIAL review found 6 defects (registry fail-open, wire-param type hole, string-ref typing, import collision,
# inline-service half-land) -> ALL FIXED + regression-tested. LIVE-CONSUMER ADOPTION (0.2.1): autotoolfactory's manifest
# converted from the legacy string form to defineSystem/defineBrand + a REAL wire (signup-grant auth->credits amount:100);
# regenerated from the PUBLISHED 0.2.1 generator -> EVERY generated file byte-identical to the legacy output EXCEPT the auth
# mount line (now carries the grant closure, mcp value byte-preserved) + 3 wire imports; tsc clean against the real modules.
# A generate.ts bug surfaced by this live run (generatePlatform pre-lowered {system,brand} -> dropped system.wire; unit tests
# only hit planPlatform directly) -> FIXED + regression-tested + republished 0.2.1. platform 82 tests pass, tsc clean.
# Ceiling 0.72 -> 0.8: the ADR-named witness (a live published-consumer adoption + the one-shot re-proof from the published
# generator) has LANDED; remaining before higher is production runtime + more community registries in the wild.
claim c053_open_service_interface_typed_2x2_opts_system_brand_split_port_capability_composition_built: Bool @>=0.8 = True
falsified_when c053_open_service_interface_typed_2x2_opts_system_brand_split_port_capability_composition_built == False
